  "output": {
    "svg": "architecture.svg",
    "medium": "documentation and notebook",
    "alt_text": "An untrusted wake event points to a server-owned checkpoint. Integrity and lifecycle checks produce verified state without authority. Current identity, policy, intent, credential, budget, and approval services feed a trusted resume reauthorization gate. A compare-and-set creates one short lease with a separate heartbeat deadline; stale owners are released and must reauthorize. A bounded executor consumes the lease for one logical operation, an external provider may commit despite a lost response, and an outcome verifier queries authoritative receipts before any retry."
